# Line endings, for task A9 of specs/03-remaining-tasks.md.
#
# The determinism gate compares emitter output byte for byte across the native
# CLI, both wasm builds and the Java binding. A CRLF introduced by a checkout on
# Windows would fail it in a way that reads like a correctness bug rather than
# like a checkout problem, so every tracked text file is pinned to LF in the
# working tree on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf happens to be set to.
#
# Verify with: python3 scripts-and-commands/check_line_endings.py

* text=auto eol=lf

# CSV fixtures carry their line endings as data, not as formatting.
# core/fixtures/generated/crlf.csv exists to prove the parser handles CRLF, and
# normalizing it would delete the thing it tests. The directory is generated and
# gitignored today; this rule is here so that publishing the fixtures later
# (specs/03-remaining-tasks.md H3.3) cannot quietly break them.
core/fixtures/generated/** -text !eol
*.csv -text !eol

# Build outputs, if one is ever tracked deliberately.
*.wasm binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
*.o binary
*.jar binary
